1
00:00:03,021 --> 00:00:04,941
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is another Ajahn Chah talk.

2
00:00:05,882 --> 00:00:07,582
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just simply called Question and Answer.

3
00:00:11,403 --> 00:00:13,444
[SPEAKER_00]: There's a few questions from somebody.

4
00:00:13,464 --> 00:00:14,104
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know who that is.

5
00:00:14,484 --> 00:00:15,584
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, Ajahn Chah answers.

6
00:00:17,565 --> 00:00:21,906
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the question... question... first question is...

7
00:00:21,946 --> 00:00:31,208
[SPEAKER_00]: There are those periods when our hearts or mind happen to be absorbed in things and become blemished or darkened, but we are still aware of ourselves.

8
00:00:31,785 --> 00:00:35,427
[SPEAKER_00]: Such as when some form of greed, hatred and delusion comes up.

9
00:00:36,748 --> 00:00:42,251
[SPEAKER_00]: Although we know that these things are objectionable, we are unable to prevent them from arising.

10
00:00:43,531 --> 00:00:55,258
[SPEAKER_00]: Could it be said that even as we are aware of them, this is providing the basis for increased clinging and attachment, and maybe is putting us further back to where we started.

11
00:00:56,544 --> 00:00:57,365
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you say that again?

12
00:00:57,805 --> 00:01:06,973
[SPEAKER_00]: Could we say... Could it be said that even as we are aware of them, this is providing the basis for increased clinging and attachment?

13
00:01:07,913 --> 00:01:08,254
[SPEAKER_01]: What is?

14
00:01:08,434 --> 00:01:10,415
[SPEAKER_01]: Their awareness of it or the thing in itself?

15
00:01:10,916 --> 00:01:11,757
[SPEAKER_00]: Being aware of it.

16
00:01:12,157 --> 00:01:13,938
[SPEAKER_01]: That's providing basis for further clinging.

17
00:01:14,038 --> 00:01:14,239
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

18
00:01:14,459 --> 00:01:14,639
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

19
00:01:14,919 --> 00:01:18,262
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe it's putting us further back to where we started from.

20
00:01:18,702 --> 00:01:18,962
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

21
00:01:19,803 --> 00:01:22,065
[SPEAKER_00]: But Ajahn Chah says... Well...

22
00:01:22,719 --> 00:01:24,580
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you read again the question from the start?

23
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,942
[SPEAKER_01]: Let me say it first and then tell me what Ajahn Chah says.

24
00:01:30,805 --> 00:01:32,306
[SPEAKER_00]: So the question begins.

25
00:01:33,006 --> 00:01:44,954
[SPEAKER_00]: There are those periods when our minds happen to be absorbed in things and become blemished or darkened, but we are still aware of ourselves, such as when some form of greed, hatred and delusion comes up.

26
00:01:45,955 --> 00:01:47,756
[SPEAKER_00]: Although we know that these things are

27
00:01:48,488 --> 00:01:49,148
[SPEAKER_00]: Objectionable.

28
00:01:49,709 --> 00:01:51,750
[SPEAKER_00]: We are unable to prevent them from arising.

29
00:01:51,810 --> 00:01:53,751
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that's it.

30
00:01:53,771 --> 00:01:55,031
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the wrong assumption there.

31
00:01:56,252 --> 00:02:02,695
[SPEAKER_01]: Trying to prevent these things from arising, which means not seeing where your responsibility is, but overdoing it.

32
00:02:02,795 --> 00:02:06,057
[SPEAKER_01]: Trying to get rid of... trying to prevent things from manifesting in the first place.

33
00:02:06,857 --> 00:02:07,738
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not on you.

34
00:02:08,178 --> 00:02:09,038
[SPEAKER_01]: That cannot be on you.

35
00:02:09,779 --> 00:02:18,023
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the response... you're... and that's why they would get confused then, and... and end up revolving around the objectionable states.

36
00:02:19,509 --> 00:02:25,133
[SPEAKER_01]: Because they're overdoing the aspect of trying to get rid of it, and that's how you bind yourself with it.

37
00:02:25,553 --> 00:02:29,216
[SPEAKER_01]: Like a dog that runs around the post, trying to get away from the post.

38
00:02:29,376 --> 00:02:30,557
[SPEAKER_01]: It's tied to the post.

39
00:02:30,657 --> 00:02:34,080
[SPEAKER_01]: Tries to get away from the post, ends up being tighter and tighter, closer to the post.

40
00:02:35,741 --> 00:02:38,303
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if that person were to recognize that they can't...

41
00:02:39,263 --> 00:02:40,024
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not up to you.

42
00:02:40,788 --> 00:02:45,570
[SPEAKER_01]: To prevent things from manifesting or not, that's not your responsibility, and that's not the problem either.

43
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:50,151
[SPEAKER_01]: But usually people believe, oh, there is greed in my mind, I must get rid of it.

44
00:02:50,692 --> 00:02:51,952
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not the problem.

45
00:02:52,392 --> 00:02:58,154
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem is you acting out of the greed, out of aversion, and that's on you.

46
00:02:58,854 --> 00:03:08,418
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have to be able to not interfere with things that has manifested on its own, and then recognize that you're not responsible for that, and that's not the issue, and that's not the greed in itself.

47
00:03:09,273 --> 00:03:11,214
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the prospect of greed being presented.

48
00:03:12,175 --> 00:03:18,580
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's you then choosing to act by body, speech or mind, delighting it, by with mental act, delighting in it, welcoming it.

49
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:19,681
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your doing.

50
00:03:20,461 --> 00:03:27,226
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when the Buddha says you shouldn't delight in greed, aversion, delusion, means that you don't delight in what has presented itself.

51
00:03:28,307 --> 00:03:31,910
[SPEAKER_01]: That doesn't mean I must get rid of what has... because that would mean that you are in control.

52
00:03:32,610 --> 00:03:34,532
[SPEAKER_01]: That you are... that you do have a say.

53
00:03:35,685 --> 00:03:37,165
[SPEAKER_01]: As to what appears, what doesn't.

54
00:03:37,806 --> 00:03:42,587
[SPEAKER_01]: But the fact that if you were to truly have a say, these things wouldn't have arisen in the first place.

55
00:03:42,647 --> 00:03:46,408
[SPEAKER_01]: But they do arise on their own, and you have no say, yet you go around acting like you have a say.

56
00:03:46,828 --> 00:03:47,028
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

57
00:03:47,048 --> 00:03:48,949
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you don't know where the problem is.

58
00:03:49,769 --> 00:03:56,571
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you think the problem is in manifestation, and not in the attitude, your attitude towards the manifestation.

59
00:03:57,271 --> 00:03:59,112
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's where the restraint comes first.

60
00:03:59,152 --> 00:04:00,592
[SPEAKER_01]: Not to prevent things from arising,

61
00:04:01,434 --> 00:04:10,421
[SPEAKER_01]: But to enable you to allow things to arise without acting out of... towards them, without acting out of it, out of that pressure of arising.

62
00:04:11,441 --> 00:04:17,306
[SPEAKER_01]: And the more restrained you are, means the less interfering with things manifestation you would be doing.

63
00:04:19,568 --> 00:04:23,030
[SPEAKER_01]: Anyway, carry on.

64
00:04:23,651 --> 00:04:25,912
[SPEAKER_00]: Anyway, Ajahn Chah answers that.

65
00:04:26,273 --> 00:04:27,313
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, that's it.

66
00:04:27,413 --> 00:04:29,295
[SPEAKER_00]: One must keep knowing them at that point.

67
00:04:29,615 --> 00:04:30,876
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the method of practice.

68
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:33,518
[SPEAKER_01]: Knowing them and the point of their arising.

69
00:04:33,919 --> 00:04:35,440
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

70
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:44,267
[SPEAKER_00]: Then the questioner asks, I mean that simultaneously we are both aware of them and repelled by them, but lacking the ability to resist them.

71
00:04:44,767 --> 00:04:49,030
[SPEAKER_00]: They just burst forth.

72
00:04:49,130 --> 00:04:52,093
[SPEAKER_01]: They can't burst forth unless you act, you choose to act out of them.

73
00:04:52,553 --> 00:04:53,494
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what they don't see.

74
00:04:53,514 --> 00:04:54,334
[SPEAKER_00]: You push them forward.

75
00:04:54,354 --> 00:04:54,455
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

76
00:04:55,175 --> 00:04:56,816
[SPEAKER_01]: The pressure might be, yeah, sure.

77
00:04:57,357 --> 00:05:01,280
[SPEAKER_01]: But no, no amount of the pressure can sort of

78
00:05:02,005 --> 00:05:02,926
[SPEAKER_01]: Make a choice for you.

79
00:05:03,806 --> 00:05:15,652
[SPEAKER_01]: It's always you who chooses to act out of the pressure, which means you can also choose not to act, which means you are the doorway through which the pressure can enter, because you are the one who opens the door, or doesn't.

80
00:05:17,894 --> 00:05:29,360
[SPEAKER_01]: Not knowing that, then, yeah, it feels like as if the action came automatically out of the pressure, because you haven't practiced restraint sufficiently enough, properly enough, so you haven't discerned that line

81
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:35,244
[SPEAKER_01]: For which you're responsible, after which, like, you don't cross.

82
00:05:35,565 --> 00:05:37,927
[SPEAKER_00]: He gives a simile.

83
00:05:38,047 --> 00:05:38,387
[SPEAKER_01]: Go for it.

84
00:05:39,388 --> 00:05:45,633
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, from then on, there will just be arising a passing away in this place.

85
00:05:45,713 --> 00:05:46,654
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

86
00:05:46,674 --> 00:05:49,056
[SPEAKER_00]: The same as waves striking the seashore.

87
00:05:49,736 --> 00:05:54,901
[SPEAKER_00]: When a wave comes in and finally reaches the shoreline, it just disintegrates and vanishes.

88
00:05:55,421 --> 00:05:57,283
[SPEAKER_00]: A new wave comes and it happens again.

89
00:05:58,083 --> 00:05:58,764
[SPEAKER_00]: The wave going

90
00:05:59,202 --> 00:06:02,183
[SPEAKER_00]: The wave going no further than the limits of the shoreline.

91
00:06:03,083 --> 00:06:07,764
[SPEAKER_00]: In the same way, nothing will be able to go beyond the limits established by one's own awareness.

92
00:06:08,625 --> 00:06:09,005
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

93
00:06:09,085 --> 00:06:10,585
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing can enter through that door.

94
00:06:11,345 --> 00:06:13,866
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you realize nothing could have ever entered.

95
00:06:14,226 --> 00:06:18,247
[SPEAKER_01]: It's you who is going out through the door and being affected by things that are outside.

96
00:06:18,767 --> 00:06:23,849
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it was you who was stepping from the shore into the water that's being hit by the waves.

97
00:06:25,549 --> 00:06:26,530
[SPEAKER_01]: That's exactly what I'm talking about.

98
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:28,130
[SPEAKER_01]: You start discerning.

99
00:06:28,827 --> 00:06:31,168
[SPEAKER_01]: Where your responsibility is, and then you don't cross it.

100
00:06:32,189 --> 00:06:37,251
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you realize the mind can arise in all shapes and forms, whatever it wants, whichever way it wants.

101
00:06:38,952 --> 00:06:39,793
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not the problem.

102
00:06:39,913 --> 00:06:41,013
[SPEAKER_01]: That never was a problem.

103
00:06:42,994 --> 00:06:45,696
[SPEAKER_01]: You welcoming it, entertaining it, trying to get rid of it.

104
00:06:46,056 --> 00:06:46,896
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where the problem is.

105
00:06:46,956 --> 00:06:53,920
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you stop doing that, means that which used to be a basis for acts of greed, still arises.

106
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:57,922
[SPEAKER_01]: But there is no greed, because greed comes from you, doesn't come from things.

107
00:06:59,381 --> 00:07:02,322
[SPEAKER_01]: That which used to be basis for ill-will, still arises.

108
00:07:03,803 --> 00:07:05,884
[SPEAKER_01]: But there is no ill-will now, in regard to it.

109
00:07:07,304 --> 00:07:09,906
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the waves still continue to come and go.

110
00:07:11,266 --> 00:07:14,748
[SPEAKER_01]: But you don't get wet anymore, because you don't go outside where the waves are.

111
00:07:15,008 --> 00:07:24,132
[SPEAKER_01]: You recognize... And people start going outside, or they carry on going outside, where you don't recognize where the safety from the wave is, as well.

112
00:07:25,014 --> 00:07:27,556
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you think I must prevent waves from coming.

113
00:07:27,636 --> 00:07:29,198
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the only way to remain dry.

114
00:07:30,359 --> 00:07:30,839
[SPEAKER_01]: But it isn't.

115
00:07:31,279 --> 00:07:36,864
[SPEAKER_01]: You just have to see the range of the wave and allow it to basically express itself, so to speak.

116
00:07:37,865 --> 00:07:38,365
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I mean.

117
00:07:38,385 --> 00:07:40,527
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to recognize things in their manifestation.

118
00:07:40,547 --> 00:07:41,788
[SPEAKER_01]: They have manifested on its own.

119
00:07:41,848 --> 00:07:43,129
[SPEAKER_01]: The wave has come on its own.

120
00:07:44,771 --> 00:07:47,393
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's you who goes there and tries to push the sea back.

121
00:07:49,058 --> 00:07:52,061
[SPEAKER_01]: That's when you... that's... basically, that's what person's question implied.

122
00:07:52,541 --> 00:07:56,865
[SPEAKER_01]: How do I... how do I, like, deal with this from arising, so it doesn't arise?

123
00:07:56,905 --> 00:08:02,790
[SPEAKER_01]: Because for him, automatically coming of the waves means automatically me walking into the water and getting wet.

124
00:08:03,811 --> 00:08:05,893
[SPEAKER_01]: He can't see the difference between the two things.

125
00:08:05,993 --> 00:08:06,693
[SPEAKER_01]: Flooded means flood.

126
00:08:06,953 --> 00:08:09,315
[SPEAKER_01]: Means flood, means wet, means soaked, drenched.

127
00:08:11,057 --> 00:08:12,138
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you were to recognize... No, no, no.

128
00:08:12,622 --> 00:08:15,564
[SPEAKER_01]: The wave can come as, like, tsunami wave.

129
00:08:16,445 --> 00:08:20,688
[SPEAKER_01]: It still can't cross this line unless I cross it that way.

130
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:21,209
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what I mean.

131
00:08:21,229 --> 00:08:23,971
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where sensory strain will enable you to start discerning that.

132
00:08:24,932 --> 00:08:31,637
[SPEAKER_01]: Without sensory strain, yeah, wave means I'm in the water, either swimming with it or trying to go against it.

133
00:08:34,139 --> 00:08:35,580
[SPEAKER_01]: So, actually, the simile is quite accurate.

134
00:08:36,901 --> 00:08:37,802
[SPEAKER_01]: The simile is quite good.

135
00:08:38,836 --> 00:08:46,241
[SPEAKER_01]: Because once you start discerning that, it's like like finding that a single doorway through which things come in because you invite them in.

136
00:08:46,621 --> 00:08:48,863
[SPEAKER_00]: Or that island that no flood can overwhelm.

137
00:08:48,883 --> 00:08:50,304
[SPEAKER_01]: The island that no flood can overwhelm.

138
00:08:50,504 --> 00:08:55,888
[SPEAKER_01]: Or as the Buddha gave the other one, the town that's surrounded by the wall and there is only one point of entry and exit.

139
00:08:56,188 --> 00:09:03,954
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, well, if I want to keep track of what's going on inside, I don't need to chase people who come in and go after people they go out.

140
00:09:03,974 --> 00:09:05,715
[SPEAKER_01]: I just need to stay at the doorway.

141
00:09:07,530 --> 00:09:14,652
[SPEAKER_01]: The doorway of that mindful context, in regard to feeling, in regard to perceptions, in regard to intentions.

142
00:09:14,672 --> 00:09:18,052
[SPEAKER_01]: Not a doorway of focusing on the tip of your nose, where you're not aware of it.

143
00:09:18,072 --> 00:09:24,754
[SPEAKER_01]: That's basically like you staring at the actual doorway, and you don't see who walks through the doorway, because you're staring at the woodwork of it.

144
00:09:26,154 --> 00:09:30,715
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you want to see, okay, whoever comes in, I know that it's him, because there's no other way of going out.

145
00:09:31,698 --> 00:09:39,821
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever manifests itself, you know it manifested to this extent, and there is lust in the mind in regard to it, or there is non-lust in regard to it.

146
00:09:39,941 --> 00:09:41,742
[SPEAKER_01]: Neither of those things are still a problem.

147
00:09:42,422 --> 00:09:51,846
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem is when you start entertaining that lust, and then welcoming it, welcoming the prospect of what that lust is pointing at, and that's how you start acting out of the desire.

148
00:09:54,587 --> 00:09:59,009
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you don't act out of desire and ill-will, those things cannot enter your mind.

149
00:09:59,610 --> 00:10:00,650
[SPEAKER_01]: Even when you actually act,

150
00:10:01,229 --> 00:10:02,509
[SPEAKER_01]: Those things can't enter your mind.

151
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:06,151
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why freedom from those things is possible in the first place.

152
00:10:06,211 --> 00:10:07,671
[SPEAKER_00]: Choice is not mine.

153
00:10:07,991 --> 00:10:08,732
[SPEAKER_00]: Choice is not mine.

154
00:10:09,352 --> 00:10:09,552
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

155
00:10:09,772 --> 00:10:17,895
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, see, people... You can eventually work your way up, whereby you see the actual present choice as not being able to be owned by you.

156
00:10:18,835 --> 00:10:25,277
[SPEAKER_01]: But until you work your way up in this gradual manner, all you're going to be doing is denying the choice after you made it.

157
00:10:26,578 --> 00:10:27,778
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's a form of determinism.

158
00:10:28,527 --> 00:10:31,928
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you made the choice, but then you say, well, there's no self, so this choice couldn't have been mine.

159
00:10:33,849 --> 00:10:35,389
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it was yours when you were making it.

160
00:10:35,569 --> 00:10:36,349
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you know that?

161
00:10:36,369 --> 00:10:39,490
[SPEAKER_01]: It was rooted in greed, or aversion, or distraction and delusion.

162
00:10:40,251 --> 00:10:45,892
[SPEAKER_01]: And whenever there is any of these three, there is the conceit, there is sense of I am, which means it is your choice.

163
00:10:47,273 --> 00:10:56,716
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the better way to go about it, not to kind of deny it in hindsight, but actually take it as a blanket rule, that the choice is always yours.

164
00:10:57,909 --> 00:11:09,398
[SPEAKER_01]: So, through that sense of responsibility for the slightest choice you make, you can then eventually overcome the ownership of the choice and responsibility with it, not remove the responsibility for the choice.

165
00:11:10,339 --> 00:11:15,323
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in order to... in order to remove the ownership of responsibility, you have to stop denying responsibility.

166
00:11:16,283 --> 00:11:20,226
[SPEAKER_01]: And people deny responsibility when they say, well, choice is not mine, nothing is mine.

167
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:25,090
[SPEAKER_01]: Or people try to deny responsibility when they try to prevent things.

168
00:11:26,031 --> 00:11:27,432
[SPEAKER_01]: They were basis for the choices.

169
00:11:28,476 --> 00:11:29,617
[SPEAKER_01]: Like the question implied.

170
00:11:31,539 --> 00:11:42,748
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as Ajahn Chah pointed out, you have to stop... Well, you have to stop engaging with things on that level, but start discerning where you're doing is, and then stop doing it.

171
00:11:42,828 --> 00:11:46,091
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's that safe shore you find, that it's inaccessible to these waves.

172
00:11:46,612 --> 00:11:54,058
[SPEAKER_01]: So, these waves remain right in front of you, coming your way at full force, but now you have confidence that they can't cross, because you know that they can't cross.

173
00:11:55,571 --> 00:11:58,333
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you stayed with it long enough and you saw that they can't cross.

174
00:12:00,195 --> 00:12:03,357
[SPEAKER_01]: If you haven't stayed with it long enough, well, you still doubt whether they can cross or not.

175
00:12:04,478 --> 00:12:06,319
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, you were affected by it.

176
00:12:07,881 --> 00:12:09,062
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you don't feel safe.

177
00:12:09,242 --> 00:12:11,363
[SPEAKER_01]: If you doubt your safety, you can't say you're safe.

178
00:12:15,246 --> 00:12:22,292
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the only way to stop doubting your safety is to discern what that safety is in regard to these things that are assailing you.

179
00:12:23,985 --> 00:12:28,448
[SPEAKER_01]: But the natural reaction is, I must prevent these things from assailing me in the first place.

180
00:12:28,488 --> 00:12:29,529
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the true safety.

181
00:12:30,329 --> 00:12:30,669
[SPEAKER_01]: It isn't.

182
00:12:31,770 --> 00:12:32,570
[SPEAKER_00]: I must destroy them.

183
00:12:32,831 --> 00:12:33,691
[SPEAKER_01]: I must destroy them.

184
00:12:33,791 --> 00:12:34,512
[SPEAKER_01]: I must...

185
00:12:34,552 --> 00:12:35,452
[SPEAKER_01]: I must remove them.

186
00:12:35,592 --> 00:12:36,773
[SPEAKER_00]: Rather than get to safety.

187
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:37,554
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

188
00:12:37,654 --> 00:12:38,414
[SPEAKER_01]: Rather than actually...

189
00:12:38,474 --> 00:12:38,855
[SPEAKER_01]: Hold on.

190
00:12:39,955 --> 00:12:42,857
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't be fighting the sea and the waves and the elements.

191
00:12:43,477 --> 00:12:47,560
[SPEAKER_01]: All I can do is find a place where those elements can't... basically can't set their foot in.

192
00:12:50,282 --> 00:12:51,843
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's when nibbāna is that negative.

193
00:12:56,797 --> 00:12:58,018
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't have to maintain it.

194
00:12:58,219 --> 00:12:58,939
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course not.

195
00:12:59,219 --> 00:13:00,260
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible to maintain it.

196
00:13:01,801 --> 00:13:02,262
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible.

197
00:13:02,362 --> 00:13:04,844
[SPEAKER_01]: Because maintenance is on the level of intention, choice.

198
00:13:05,584 --> 00:13:07,886
[SPEAKER_01]: And this is safe in regard to...

199
00:13:08,366 --> 00:13:09,027
[SPEAKER_01]: Remember it.

200
00:13:09,427 --> 00:13:09,547
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

201
00:13:09,827 --> 00:13:12,249
[SPEAKER_01]: You discern it in regard to the threat.

202
00:13:13,450 --> 00:13:14,891
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it requires no maintenance.

203
00:13:15,472 --> 00:13:18,434
[SPEAKER_01]: Because any manifestation is a threat.

204
00:13:19,915 --> 00:13:23,738
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means safety is in regard to any threat.

205
00:13:24,415 --> 00:13:26,276
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means it's in regard to any manifestation.

206
00:13:26,936 --> 00:13:35,559
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's the independent manifestation of thing, which is not your doing, that maintains your sense of safety, which is equally not your doing.

207
00:13:36,039 --> 00:13:39,560
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why arahantship is effortless, once you develop it.

208
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:41,601
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you only need manifestation.

209
00:13:41,761 --> 00:13:54,145
[SPEAKER_01]: You only need to work, initially, to stop obscuring the true nature of manifestations, that it cannot be owned, because of that it's impermanent, that it's unsatisfactory, because it doesn't have that

210
00:13:56,892 --> 00:13:59,213
[SPEAKER_01]: Sense of pleasure connected with mastery over things.

211
00:14:00,013 --> 00:14:01,434
[SPEAKER_01]: And because of that, it cannot be yours.

212
00:14:02,374 --> 00:14:03,214
[SPEAKER_01]: Hence, it's not self.

213
00:14:04,255 --> 00:14:15,359
[SPEAKER_00]: There's always... then that manifestation, discerning a thing, it reveals all the time that safe zone.

214
00:14:15,619 --> 00:14:15,799
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

215
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:16,700
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the thing.

216
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:19,901
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you fully understood it, you don't have to keep discerning it.

217
00:14:20,021 --> 00:14:20,241
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

218
00:14:20,941 --> 00:14:24,683
[SPEAKER_01]: The only... like an ārya, sāvaka, needs to keep discerning it.

219
00:14:25,311 --> 00:14:31,776
[SPEAKER_01]: Because he still has residues of habits of ignorance and lust and so on.

220
00:14:31,816 --> 00:14:40,624
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he has to keep going against that grain until it's fully purified and then there is nothing with the grain anymore.

221
00:14:40,644 --> 00:14:47,369
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm just saying this so people don't develop... like Arahant is just constantly, this is a manifestation, this is a manifestation... No.

222
00:14:47,409 --> 00:14:49,951
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever you're aware of, it has been manifested.

223
00:14:49,971 --> 00:14:51,753
[SPEAKER_01]: To that extent, you're fully aware of it already.

224
00:14:52,453 --> 00:14:54,555
[SPEAKER_01]: And to that extent, you're fully free from it already.

225
00:14:54,929 --> 00:14:57,050
[SPEAKER_01]: Because there was nothing to affect you in the first place.

226
00:14:58,330 --> 00:15:06,073
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's think, well, and Aryan, then, would... you're aware of that... it reveals the island.

227
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:07,093
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

228
00:15:07,493 --> 00:15:08,033
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly.

229
00:15:08,053 --> 00:15:10,174
[SPEAKER_00]: The island is revealed by the waves.

230
00:15:10,894 --> 00:15:11,114
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

231
00:15:12,235 --> 00:15:12,755
[SPEAKER_00]: So all you need is...

232
00:15:12,775 --> 00:15:15,516
[SPEAKER_01]: The island is outlined by the sea.

233
00:15:15,536 --> 00:15:15,636
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

234
00:15:16,796 --> 00:15:18,397
[SPEAKER_00]: So... Yeah.

235
00:15:19,252 --> 00:15:24,675
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the unborn, like if the sea is born, nibbāna is the unborn, the unmanifested.

236
00:15:25,035 --> 00:15:32,139
[SPEAKER_01]: So, from whatever is manifested, nibbāna is outlined by being the opposite of that.

237
00:15:32,219 --> 00:15:35,581
[SPEAKER_01]: Undefined, undesignated, undetermined.

238
00:15:35,882 --> 00:15:36,042
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

239
00:15:38,463 --> 00:15:41,785
[SPEAKER_00]: And by recognizing that, you can't unrecognize it.

240
00:15:41,985 --> 00:15:42,405
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

241
00:15:42,565 --> 00:15:42,705
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

242
00:15:42,805 --> 00:15:45,847
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't go back the other way and pretend you haven't recognized it.

243
00:15:45,987 --> 00:15:48,048
[SPEAKER_00]: You haven't recognized the extent of manifestation.

244
00:15:48,389 --> 00:15:48,569
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

245
00:15:48,789 --> 00:15:48,909
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

246
00:15:49,357 --> 00:15:51,438
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that is the true nature of manifestations.

247
00:15:52,558 --> 00:15:53,418
[SPEAKER_01]: They cannot be owned.

248
00:15:54,398 --> 00:15:55,539
[SPEAKER_01]: They cannot be pleasurable.

249
00:15:56,479 --> 00:15:57,999
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you cannot be your own.

250
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:01,180
[SPEAKER_01]: That is the true nature.

251
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:08,842
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why liberation from the ownership, this sense of self and the dependence on pleasure is possible.

252
00:16:09,262 --> 00:16:12,183
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you actually get to discern and then these things become inconceivable.

253
00:16:12,743 --> 00:16:18,645
[SPEAKER_01]: If those things were not truly beyond ownership, unpleasant,

254
00:16:19,867 --> 00:16:20,768
[SPEAKER_01]: Not your sense of self.

255
00:16:21,288 --> 00:16:22,609
[SPEAKER_01]: They can't be maintained in regard to it.

256
00:16:22,689 --> 00:16:25,251
[SPEAKER_01]: If they were not truly like that, you wouldn't be able to free yourself from it.

257
00:16:26,232 --> 00:16:28,954
[SPEAKER_01]: The sense of self would be the master and owner of the experience.

258
00:16:29,454 --> 00:16:31,636
[SPEAKER_01]: But that means there wouldn't be any problems or suffering.

259
00:16:31,876 --> 00:16:36,259
[SPEAKER_01]: But the fact that there is a problem of suffering, means the sense of ownership is incompatible with that.

260
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:43,004
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why human existence is a discrepancy between how things actually are and how you're acting them to be.

261
00:16:43,985 --> 00:16:45,606
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is why you're responsible for their being.

262
00:16:48,345 --> 00:16:58,572
[SPEAKER_01]: Discrepancy, dukkha... Any degree of discrepancy determines the degree of liability towards the dukkha.

263
00:16:59,933 --> 00:17:02,475
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no discrepancy, no base for dukkha.

264
00:17:02,715 --> 00:17:03,355
[SPEAKER_01]: That's arahant.

265
00:17:05,116 --> 00:17:06,537
[SPEAKER_01]: Actually, in the scene, there's just the scene.

266
00:17:07,818 --> 00:17:08,619
[SPEAKER_01]: A is just A.

267
00:17:08,719 --> 00:17:09,699
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no discrepancy there.

268
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:14,663
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, the people sometimes get the sense of it, but then they look for the discrepancy at the wrong place.

269
00:17:14,803 --> 00:17:17,765
[SPEAKER_01]: They look at the discrepancy in the A, and they try to

270
00:17:18,295 --> 00:17:20,176
[SPEAKER_01]: Resolve A of discrepancy.

271
00:17:20,816 --> 00:17:25,637
[SPEAKER_01]: The scene must be resolved of the lust and aversion, delusion, of the discrepancy of it.

272
00:17:25,697 --> 00:17:25,997
[SPEAKER_01]: But no.

273
00:17:26,618 --> 00:17:28,678
[SPEAKER_01]: Lust and aversion, delusion is not in the scene.

274
00:17:30,099 --> 00:17:31,259
[SPEAKER_01]: It's in your attitude towards it.

275
00:17:31,899 --> 00:17:34,520
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where you remove that kind of attitude.

276
00:17:34,540 --> 00:17:35,620
[SPEAKER_01]: You undo it.

277
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:37,141
[SPEAKER_01]: You extinguish it.

278
00:17:38,301 --> 00:17:42,762
[SPEAKER_01]: And then what you have is in the scene, there's just the scene.

279
00:17:43,763 --> 00:17:45,023
[SPEAKER_01]: In the herd, there's just the herd.

280
00:17:47,708 --> 00:17:48,949
[SPEAKER_00]: Smell, taste, touch, same.

281
00:17:49,369 --> 00:17:50,010
[SPEAKER_00]: Thought, thought.

282
00:17:52,632 --> 00:17:57,836
[SPEAKER_01]: But what person's question implied is, oh, there is a scene of greed, aversion, delusion.

283
00:17:57,876 --> 00:17:59,357
[SPEAKER_01]: How do I prevent it from being seen?

284
00:18:01,258 --> 00:18:08,083
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he didn't see, he doesn't see that the issue was in his attitude towards the scene, not the scene.

285
00:18:09,004 --> 00:18:16,830
[SPEAKER_01]: So, his question of trying to deal with the scene, prevent it, make it not, make it unmanifest,

286
00:18:18,242 --> 00:18:22,020
[SPEAKER_01]: imply the wrong view of him looking at the solution in the wrong place.

